tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:13:16-08:00","id":1058098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1058089#post1058089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Photoshop? What tools?</div> </div> </div> </div>GIMP. Smudge tool at ~90% rate to remove the nails (drag the surrounding colors over the nails to erase them), then Free Select, at 4-800% zoom to draw an outline for the cloth parts and move them to a new layer (with free select, use small line segments rather than trying to follow a curve by hand). Then Colorize, fiddling with the settings until it looked good (in this case, ~5/44/0).<br /> <br /> The free select is the slowest part, since you have to do detailed selection around things like each bead on the abacus. It took... half an hour or so, I think? Would take longer if I weren't familiar with the process. I used to do this a lot for my games, finding pictures that worked well then changing the hair and eye color to match the character I wanted to use them for.<br /> <br /> Have an image you want recolored / tweaked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 03-04-2017, 02:16 