edby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T19:26:37-07:00","id":1065056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1065030#post1065030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Darn it. I had written a nice big summary... and then the forum ate it. Grr. Will try again after dinner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I write all my long posts in Word or Google Docs before posting. I don't trust the forum software.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T19:46:42-07:00","id":1065060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1065056#post1065056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I write all my long posts in Word or Google Docs before posting. I don't trust the forum software.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually do too. &gt;.&gt; Just... forgot this time. Oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T20:23:00-07:00","id":1065069,"title":"","content":"I'm sure wonderandawe's notes cover the NPCs, but wanted to give my own take on Aisa's caste of characters as well.<br /> <br /> Important NPCs:<ul><li>Ragara Zara - Ryu's daughter, recently exalted as water aspect while surviving Mnemon's assassination attempt. Was previously Aisa's handmaiden, now a student at the Heptagram. Aisa thinks of her as a protege, and adores her.</li> <li>V'Neef Iphen - Childhood friend. He was in love with Aisa, but she recently broke his heart, and turns out she cared for him more than she thought she did. Knows about her plans to oppose Mnemon / take the throne.</li> <li>Ai'Zul and Jal'Kaith - Retainers. Air and Earth elementals respectively. Flighty+curious spy/messenger and serious fatherly bodyguard.</li> <li>Mnemon Duhalva - Recently elevated Domine of the Heptagram. Aisa's ally, but mostly uninterested in politics. Brilliant researcher.</li> <li>Cathak Nadrian - Cathak Cainan's son. Charming, handsome, almost as well bred as Aisa. They despise each other, but are considering engagement regardless. Sidereal prophecy (which only Aisa knows) that if they marry they'll found a house as great as Mnemon, but one will end up killing the other.</li> <li>Tepet Rowep - Legionaire seeking Aisa's hand (and she's considering it). Probably prompted to do so by his mortal sister, who (sidereal prophecy again) loves or could love Aisa (and it could be mutual).</li> <li>Anuli - Independent Sidereal, she and Aisa are becoming friends. In contrast to two bronze faction observers at the Heptagram (one posing as a professor, the other an immaculate monk)</li> <li>V'Neef - Has met with Aisa repeatedly. They get along reasonably well, and Aisa has associated herself with this house pretty publicly. Doesn't know she seeks the throne, but Aisa thinks V'Neef will be firmly on her side.</li> <li>Unnamed Tepet Elders - Have met with Aisa, and she's promised to act on their behalf. She's mediated an important deal for them, protected the Roseblack from Mnemon, and otherwise is busy getting them firmly in her debt. But honestly so - no manipulation there, just genuinely helping out a desperate house. They don't know she seeks the throne yet.</li> <li>Cynis Belar - One of the three leaders of the house. Was in Mnemon's camp, but supporting Aisa and opposing Mnemon on her behalf (secretly for now) pending full approval of a list of economic concessions from a new Empress.</li> <li>Cathak Cainan - Hasn't supported any candidate yet because they were all too secular and more interested in fighting than preserving the Realm. Last month Aisa met with him, and while he hasn't pledged anything, she's winning him over because she's genuinely pious and cares more about Creation than about herself.</li> <li>Aisa's parents (unnamed) - Her father (from Sessus) was recently poisoned because he tried to keep her secrets. Her mother, from Mnemon, was probably the poisoner, and just this month told Mnemon, and either poisoned her husband or allowed someone else to do it.</li> <li>Mnemon - Just recently learned that Aisa, far from being a loyal and effective supporter (which illusion she'd maintained successfully), is actively opposing her. Hasn't yet had time to act on that knowledge, other than to try and assassinate Zara.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Upcoming plans:<ul><li>Tell V'Neef and Tepet about her plans for the throne, and get their opinions on the coming civil war.</li> <li>Solidify her relations with Cathak Cainan and House Cynis. Feel out the other great houses.</li> <li>Meet with Ledaal Kes and convince him not to compete with her.</li> <li>Consolidate her hold on the Heptagram and surrounding area to build a safe base of operations.</li> <li>Survive Mnemon's coming wrath.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:24:41-07:00","id":1065359,"title":"","content":"I'll follow Bluewinds and write something similar, also this an excuse for me to make a list of the the npc's in my area.<br /> <br /> NPC's of note:<br /> -Darkest Dawn: Full moon lunar with a Snow lion totem. Working on him becoming an ally by making society more tolerant of his existence. So far others<br /> see him as a weapon I can kinda control.<br /> <br /> -Ferem Helkar: Quelaana's uncle and fire aspected admiral. Currently held hostage by Mneumon's fleet. This is an obscure canon character in the<br /> dragon-blooded book.<br /> <br /> -Florivet: 2nd circle Lemon and warden of Helkar's imprisonment.<br /> <br /> -Gold faction Sidereal(name unknown): Quelaana knows very little about the Sidickery in the area but will recognize him on sight and is very suspicious of<br /> him.<br /> <br /> - Ejava Tepet &quot;Roseblack&quot;: Currently occupying Amber River and ally to Quelaana. Mnemon currently has a fleet blockading Amber river to eventually<br /> starve them out. Land trade routes are making this a time consuming affair.<br /> <br /> -Peleps Hideki: Magistrate Spymaster and Quelaana's superior. We've been forgetting this guy exists to be honest, so he doesn't have much character<br /> progression. Sent me to the Gold Faction Sidereal so probably has gold faction eyes on him as well.<br /> <br /> -Hymn of solace: God of theatrical fighting and mentor of Quelaana. He's often busy juggling all his students across creation so he's rarely around. God of<br /> Fourth Rank if that matters.<br /> <br /> -Bull of the North: Has sent an emissary to Inara and is trying to get them to turn on the Realm. Hasn't done anything directly yet.<br /> <br /> -Rorick: The Bull's emissary and has agreed to a temporary non-aggression pact with Quelaana.<br /> <br /> -Bloody Hand: Extremist anti-slavery group in the slave coast that has been recently freed from slavery in Amber River. They're having a hard time<br /> refocusing after their victory.<br /> <br /> -Rei: Stealth based henchman that is easily forgotten because she's quiet. I'm debating if I want her to end up a ronin or not.<br /> <br /> -Mai: Performance/martial arts henchman that helps out on stage. She tends to be a rumor monger and knows more about pelagials than most people should.<br /> <br /> -Yuuta: Prop master and the straight man of the group. He's gotten crotchedy and very good at making wooden weapons as they break all the time in<br /> sparring.<br /> <br /> <br /> Upcoming plans:<br /> -Free Helkar and break the Blockade somehow.<br /> -Search for the warstriders that fell through the ice.<br /> -Get Inara as an ally despite the Bull of the North's attempts.<br /> -Finalize Darkest Dawn as an ally( finding stuff to do with him is proving difficult).<br /> -Deal with Amber River's drug addiction and Cynis being pricks still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:44:20-07:00","id":1066605,"title":"","content":"This is good stuff! I got some GM notes too which I'm gonna rewrite a bit to taste and will try get started as soon as I can. Who's still playing who hasn't spoken up yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T17:37:13-07:00","id":1066646,"title":"","content":"Will add my own as well:<br /> <br /> Important NPCs:<ul><li>V'neef Bilar: Keeper of the Imperial Manse. Akashan has convinced her to allow him to do experiments on the manse out of mutual hate for Mnemnon. He has no actual respect for her and has used her naked ambition to con her into helping with various other plans around the Imperial City under the guise of manse investigations.</li> <li>Ledaal Zhan: Akashan's elder brother, House of Bells Graduate, bit of a chip on his shoulder, poster boy for biomagitech use, recently reconciled with his brother. Being groomed to lead the biomagitech enhanced special forces group Akashan is putting together. That group has no formal name yet, but consists of DB of proven loyalty receptive to augmentation who have started to receive biomagitech.</li> <li>Ledaal Leadership: Generally in favor of Akashan's plans but cautious about throwing too many resources into it.</li> <li>Cynis Leadership: Akashan helped the exchange of territory by entering into an agreement where their wood aspects help him with plant based artifacts.</li> <li>(Adeptus Ledaalicus): No formal name yet. A group of Ledaal crafters bolstered by talent poached from other houses by marriage as well as from the Threshold and Lost Eggs. The core group are sympathetic to Akashan's ideas about self-enhancement with artifacts. Strong oaths of secrecy and sorcery bind them to not reveal information about his secret craft charms and techniques. Recently had a bit of a struggle over their desire to collaborate outside the group but Akashan's arguments prevailed. One was particularly vocal in opposition.</li> <li>Ledaal Kes: Effectively Akashan's boss. Connection to the Sidereals who is seeking the throne himself as part of a plan to counter the Deathlords. A bit worried that Akashan's plans for Ledaal will turn them into the craft version of Sesus.</li> <li>Ascending Stratum: Jadeborn Artisan and Akashan's lover. Commands a smallish colony under Akashan's manse and his connection to the Conclave (Jadeborn leadership)</li> <li>Fulminous Heart: Akashan's Jadeborn mentor and crafting instructor. Master of a powerful underground factory cathedral and well respected as a crafter.</li> <li>Jadeborn Conclave: Partners with Akashan on artifact research. Work with him to develop new food preparation methods to allow Ledaal to corner the market on supplying long voyages and the legions in the field. Also, recently developed an artifact that allows the transfers of essence from those in safe places to others far away. Currently there is an arrangement where Ledaal trades food surplus (allowing the JB to carve more soldiers and focus more on manufacturing) in exchange for rare materials and finished goods.</li> <li>Xochiquetzal: Raptok Dragon King plant magic specialist. She is working as a supplier for Akashan's artifact crafting and is helping to teach other DK the necessary techniques. Her cooperation is contingent on an Eclipse Oath to arrange periodic meetings with Ryo as well as Akashan putting Ledaal resources and Sidereal information to find and bring together civilized and feral DKs.</li> <li>Peleps Hiro: Owns a broken factory cathedral near the Imperial City. Akashan and Ryo have been trying to ruin it so they can seize the place. Akashan is starting to consider having him killed.</li> </ul>Upcoming Plans:<ul><li>Retrofit an undercapped Wood Manse somewhere in the Arjuf Dominion. Would be built to support Jadeborn food operations below the surface to take advantage of their magic and benefit it with enhanced fertility, provide ideal growing conditions for Xochiquetzal's plant based artifacts and DK operations, and to keep the Cynis gardeners somewhere he can keep an eye on them. Rough plans suggest even without any of those three it could substantually improve food production in the Dominion.</li> <li>&quot;Acquire&quot; Peleps Hiro's manse and put it back into operation.</li> <li>Continue expanding and consolidating his group of crafters and enhanced special forces.</li> <li>Find a way to open the Imperial Manse (He got some V'Neef sorcerers killed recently with his last attempt. V'neef Bilar was ecstatic that they got it to do something)</li> <li>Finish setting up forces and supplies in the Imperial City in preparation for the battle for the Manse when it opens. (He already did a detailed survey of the place, drew up plans for attack and defense, and figured out how to get the Scarlet Stone, 100 veteran Jadeborn warriors, on their side when the fighting starts)</li> <li>Build a fleet of ships to break the blockade in the North and allow him to study the geomancy of Whitewall (Before redeploying to the West to check the power of the Silver Prince)</li> <li>Get an Exotic Material Component supply chain up and running to keep up with all his crafting. (Right now he is trading with the Jadeborn in small amounts, using DK 1 dot artifacts as components in small amounts, and has some being imported through the conspiracy in small amounts.</li> <li>Bring Kes around to support Aisa (Right now Kes got the Sids to lend Akashan a hidden factory cathedral so he could make anti-deathlord artifacts. They let him have access to the plans for non-doomsday, non-fast transport, non-medical artifacts)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Now, the craft problem. I have really optimized crafting pools and lots of assistants for extra successes. I also have a custom speed multiplication charm, a hearthstone that doubles speed, and a lot of money. Now the Sid's lent me a Factory Cathedral and we should have another up and working soon. My subordinates probably can't craft Artifact 4+, but there are a lot of useful E3s.<br /> <br /> wonderandawe and I agreed that we didn't want my crafting to dominate the game and overshadow the actions of the other players. We were trying crafting slots. Effectively they work like project slots in 3E, each one allows you to be working on one artifact at time and they get built at a rate of 1 dot per week like other backgrounds. Each speed multiplier multiplies slots instead. So the Season-&gt;Month conversion of a Factory Cathedral tripled mine to 6. My hearthstone doubled it again to 12. My charm triples it again to 36. In this system FCs don't produce artifacts in <br /> <br /> We were still deciding what was reasonable to put into craft slots. I had suggested that manses might not be a good idea since then I could produce more Factory-Cathedrals. We were also deciding if Artifact N/A were on the table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-22-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:55:54-07:00","id":1067239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1066646#post1066646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were also deciding if Artifact N/A were on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can solve that one quickly, no absolutely not.<br /> <br /> It sounds like the GM got real crazy on the crafting thing, I'm more of a fan of the rules light level of play but I'll work out something suitably fun for this level of rule bending insanity. I'm sure there's a very good reason the Sidereals a Factory Cathedral to what seems to be a fairly mad scientist and when I work out what it is that'll be fun!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:48:35-07:00","id":1067364,"title":"","content":"They wanted me to build things for the war on the Deathlords and I am one of the few people who can craft Artifact 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:28:52-07:00","id":1067513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067364#post1067364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wanted me to build things for the war on the Deathlords and I am one of the few people who can craft Artifact 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you all fairly middlin' Dragonbloods? That sounds kind of crazy<br /> <br /> Also want to keep the game about Realm Politics so Deathlords likely won't be a thing unless someone literally dies and wants to keep playing anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:07:16-07:00","id":1067660,"title":"","content":"Exthalion is embellishing what he was allowed. He's dependent on schematics to build stuff and most of the crazy/first age stuff is off limits. Exthalion is the one investigating the Deathlord foreshadowing stuff so he does get a fair amount of leeway, but being able to build artifact 5's and knowing how to build a specific artifact 5 is very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:40:02-07:00","id":1067680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fansibubbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067513#post1067513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't you all fairly middlin' Dragonbloods? That sounds kind of crazy<br /> <br /> Also want to keep the game about Realm Politics so Deathlords likely won't be a thing unless someone literally dies and wants to keep playing anyway</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There were artifacts involved to meet the trait minimums. The Deathlord thing wasn't my idea, and IC Akashan has just been using it as a pretense to get Kes to support his plans. For example, to get Kes to agree to support him in breaking the blockade Akashan's excuse was that he wanted to go study Whitewall with its wards against the dead. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067660#post1067660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion is embellishing what he was allowed. He's dependent on schematics to build stuff and most of the crazy/first age stuff is off limits. Exthalion is the one investigating the Deathlord foreshadowing stuff so he does get a fair amount of leeway, but being able to build artifact 5's and knowing how to build a specific artifact 5 is very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not embellishing in the least.<br /> <br /> As far as crafting is concerned, I am dependent on nothing. Half of the successes required to craft an artifact come from the design work. If you have the templates you do not have to generate those successes yourself and effectively cut the required successes in half. However, you must reuse the exact Exotic Material Components. I asked about usable first age templates because First Age Solars had the Art of Permanence and Design Beyond Limit which could be encoded into templates. I also pointed out, when I first asked wonderandawe about them, that most of them probably use Wyld Shaped EMCs and so wouldn't be usable to me. Wonderandawe (do you capitalize a username at the start of a sentence) was the one who set the templates the Sids gave me access to after IC PM negotiation with them.If nothing else, I literally invented a new kind of artifact in game. <br /> <br /> Wonderandawe is also the one who created the Deathlord connection. It was brought up the first time Akashan interacted with Kes and was the explicit motivation wonderandawe gave for the Sidereals loaning out the FC. We also discussed how much Akashan could squeeze in personal projects on the side and get away with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However, since I am apparently at the place where the Craft rules start to break the game there was much discussion over how they were going to work from now on. To be fair, I invested large portions of my character resources and IC activities on getting to this point.<br /> <br /> It would be a houserule if I needed existing templates for Artifact 5 and couldn't produce them myself. I do not mind houseruling to limit the power of Crafting if it improves the enjoyment of everyone. But I did not distort the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:42:22-07:00","id":1067682,"title":"","content":"But yes, I think 'fairly middling' may be somewhat generous. We're starting characters with 30xp and 10 extra dots of backgrounds (In my case, nearly all Allies). I just bought E4 and am saving up for a presence excellency to make difficulty 4 checks more reliable - not exactly high-powered stuff going on in my corner of the world. ^^;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 03-24-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:50:19-07:00","id":1067717,"title":"","content":"The crafting stuff seems way out of control to be honest, even for a Solar campaign it's sounding OTT and I'm not really sure how much challenge anything would be with that level of power in the field.<br /> <br /> The Realm doesn't really make Artifact 5's, they treasure the few that remain. If we're at &quot;My character is making first age miracles&quot; with only 30xp the rules really haven't been treated kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:52:12-07:00","id":1067719,"title":"","content":"I think my character is mechanically the most powerful since I'm using the immaculate template, but combat has proven to only be an okay option in a macro style game. I'm finding myself having to constantly make allies to be able to keep fighting my enemies without dying horribly. I can take other dragon-blooded single handedly in combat but even with dreaming pearl it's exhausting and I'm usually mote tapped because tiny mote pool. Our big strength is our ability to ally people to our cause because of the background rules.<br /> <br /> Actually now that I think about I could use a presence excellency too. The prism of focused passion is a really good Band-Aid for my lack of excellencies.<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't think Wonder realized how optimized Exthalion was at crafting. On paper a factory cathedral is a good way to make a crafting character involved with politics. Something will likely need to be nerfed/messed. The craft slot multiplication was a Band-Aid to keep craft speed enhancer's relevant so that's probably a good place to start. Maybe we go like DnD crits and multipliers add onto one another instead of multiplying. so a x3 and a x2 multiplier would make a total of x4. basically making each multiplier an extra 2 crafting slots. The base number of crafting slots could be one if this is still too big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","user":"Eura","date":". 03-24-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:25:06-07:00","id":1067763,"title":"","content":"Some notes on crafting:<br /> <br /> Crafting is worthless until it is gamebreaking. Without speed multipliers a character is lucky to craft one artifact in the entire game. With speed multipliers I have seen craft intervals of minutes. (That was a Solar, and they have better speed charms than everyone else)<br /> <br /> The great restriction is Exotic Material Components. There are basically no rules for them at all and each one can be its own little quest to go find. The way around this is to use artifacts. An artifact one dot lower than the one you are trying to build can be substituted for an EMC. This comes to over 200 Artifact 1s per Artifact 5. First Age production levels were only possible because they had world-spanning collection and transportation infrastructure to keep the FCs supplied with EMCs and artifact components.<br /> <br /> I do not have and Ledaal could not afford to keep me supplied with as many EMCs as I would need.<br /> <br /> My way around this was the Dragon Kings. They have two different charms that let them make an Artifact 1 in a scene. However, this does not solve all my problems. Combining these Artifact 1s into progressively higher level components all take time. Months for every step if we keep to the Craft Slot system. Assuming I have enough crafters to rope into it, it would take 5+4+3+2=14 months to make 1 Artifact 5 from scratch.(1)<br /> <br /> Solars get Design Beyond Limit. This is HUGE in its impact because it pushes artifacts down on level for purposes of crafting. Which means an Artifact 5 would require 4 Artifact 3 components instead of 5 Artifact 4 components. That saves massive amounts of time and material. Art of Permanence + DBL means that for the same cost as modern artificers pay they could craft stuff that doesn't require maintenance, simplifying their supply chains enormously. <br /> <br /> (1) Its actually worse with batches since being able to make a whole bunch of artifacts likewise increases the number of components you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:48:07-07:00","id":1067798,"title":"","content":"If your views on Crafting are its either worthless or gamebreaking it might be best to roll up something new because neither sound much fun for anybody.<br /> <br /> I mean if you're just here to try break the game mechanically then I'm sorry to say I'm not really in for that. I got pitched on this being a talky, schemey political game!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:19:36-07:00","id":1067811,"title":"","content":"Should I start formatting posts differently? It feels like my points are being lost. Most of the last one was explaining how Craft wouldn't be gamebreaking and giving you levers to reign it in.<br /> <br /> I think the letters I have written clearly demonstrate I am not just here to break the game. Pre-human relations, the Realm's cultural lionization of warriors at the expense of artifice and sorcery, the squalor of the Second Age compared to the Shogunate, Akashan's political marriage, the struggle for the soul of House Ledaal, and the like all show that I don't just want to churn out Five-Metal Shrikes until I am god-emperor of Creation.<br /> <br /> Crafting is a complex subsystem that does not reward dabbling. Especially DB crafting where all their native magic does is break things. (1) It was apparently balanced around the assumption that it gives you backgrounds without spending XP and so is filled with mechanical and lore speedbumps. I have finally gotten over most of them and it has taken politics and adventure to do so.<br /> <br /> However! I was trying to set myself up to facilitate other people's ambitions. I wanted to start working on sorcery artifacts for Aisa, Gunzosha armor for the conspiracy's troops (2), etc. My work in the Imperial City is because I assume there is going to be a fight there with conspiracy members and their retainers on one side and various other factions on the other. <br /> <br /> One person cannot attune to an infinite amount of artifacts or even use all that many even if they could. None of the military skyships I am able to craft are particularly threatening on a strategic scale except for moving troops I don't have. None of the ships really come with guns. What is more, all the other factions have more Dragonblooded! The conspiracy is small and we need force multipliers if we are going to win on anything other than Imperial Manse fiat. The allies the others have been gathering are part of that. I was hoping to be another.<br /> <br /> <br /> What are your setting and mechanical assumptions regarding artifacts so I can know what would make you comfortable?<br /> <br /> <br /> (1) An exaggeration, but not much of one.<br /> (2) Since I don't have any and have made no effort to get an army or navy that is personally loyal to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:50:06-07:00","id":1067825,"title":"","content":"Yesterday you were trying to get the ok for building artifact N/A's and not too long ago you were trying the same thing for artifact 5's. The 1-3 artifact range is what's readily acceptable for crafting assuming you have the schematics and materials. Artifact 4-5 will require questing for but isn't an outright no as long as your willing to work for it. Nobody is saying you can't craft or contribute. I would like to point out a factory cathedral can also build mundane things so a mundane ship fleet is doable if extremely time consuming (not that bad when compared to artifacts though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:18:00-07:00","id":1067833,"title":"","content":"Wait I'm confused, did you mean this or not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067763#post1067763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some notes on crafting:<br /> <br /> Crafting is worthless until it is gamebreaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your first question to me was if N/A artifacts were on the table. You're giving me limitations on crafting and also how you've gotten around them so I'm really lost as to what point you think you're making here.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to be allowing the pumping out of Artifact 5 items. If that's where the campaign is at well we're going to have to work something out in the transition to fix that, because it's a bit silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:56:10-07:00","id":1067869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fansibubbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067833#post1067833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait I'm confused, did you mean this or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a point of the very next sentence qualifying what that meant. If you must invest in 3 abilities and 3 attributes, multiple charms, as well as background dots to roll dice once in an entire campaign then craft is worthless because the dots on your sheet are doing nothing. If, after you jump through all those hoops, the ST doesn't like what you want to make then it is &quot;gamebreaking&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fansibubbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067833#post1067833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your first question to me was if N/A artifacts were on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That post was over a thousand words long and<i> I didn't ask</i>. I literally said &quot;We were also deciding if Artifact N/A were on the table.&quot; In PMs with wonderandawe my suggested N/A were putting larger than normal essence cannons on a first age hull and building a skyship larger than a warbird but smaller than Skywolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fansibubbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1067833#post1067833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're giving me limitations on crafting and also how you've gotten around them so I'm really lost as to what point you think you're making here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I not include the part where my &quot;getting around the limitation&quot; and &quot;pumping out&quot; came to 14 months each with nothing else being crafted? I feel like I did. In the very post you are quoting in fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Before I type out the arguments I have, would you just rather I didn't? The others deserve a good experience and if all I am doing is souring you on the idea of STing then it isn't fair to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-24-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:32:34-07:00","id":1067881,"title":"","content":"I would just rather you didn't, if you've got this far in and don't see a problem with what you've done to make craft 'viable' I'm not really sure I'm going to convince you. Your character's ability is so ridiculously out of scale with the rest of the party and Dragonblooded in general it'd be a massive drag.<br /> <br /> I know Crafting is a bit junkrat as a DB, but that's kind of thematic. Your better off looting and fixing up the long forgotten past than building stuff fresh, it's what I did when I had an Air DB Crafter a good few years ago. The DB are pretty good at repair and heck the party might even be coming into some fucked up Warstriders sooner rather than later. The DB charmset being full of flawed gems is pretty much a universal thing and not something you're really meant to &quot;fix&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:07:02-07:00","id":1067897,"title":"","content":"Please accept my respectful request to withdraw from this game.<br /> <br /> I wish you all the best and hope you continue to enjoy playing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:16:30-07:00","id":1067985,"title":"","content":"Best of luck!<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the rest, post will be going up today. Will use Titus for it as we've not quite worked out what to do with Ryo yet. You can all no doubt guess he is quite busy right now though!<br /> <br /> After it's up people can PM me with what they plan to do and also anything they'd like to see some feedback/return on that they've done in the past. It'll be a little stumbling to get going but I'm sure we'll manage.<br /> <br /> Will roll out a new OOC soon so I have edit privileges for the starting posts and XP charts but that isn't urgent.All okay?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:17:13-07:00","id":1068091,"title":"","content":"Question: Are we doing pm's for Resplendent or Ascending Wood? Bluewinds and I have sent letters for Ascending wood before the debacle happened, so would we technically have 4 more exp than the rest of the party?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:47:11-07:00","id":1068277,"title":"","content":"I suspect PMs are for Resplendent Wood now; I just need to write up what I already had going with wonderandawe for an Ascending Wood letter and then all three of us (there are now three of us, after all) will be caught up.<br /> <br /> Right! I needed to write a thing for you!<br /> <br /> NPCs:<ul><li>Francesco Contarini - Carmela's great-grandfather. Patriarch of House Contarini, a family of Threshold Dragon-Bloods, merchants and bankers and traders and financiers and generally people who sully themselves with money. They are not Imperial unless you squint real hard, but they do constantly poach whatever qualified people they can find and have a number of Imperial Dragons in their lineage. Francesco has ambitions of using the Realm Civil War to put his family into Imperial House levels of wealth and influence.</li> <li>Nemias Contarini (Iselsi Nemias) - Carmela's father, an exiled Iselsi who married into the Contarini family. May or may not still be an All-Seeing Eye agent, but either way still maintains a certain degree of loyalty and contacts regarding the Realm. Sent Carmela to look after...</li> <li>Geno Husumori - Magistrate of the Pahua Basin, together with his Archons HE IS THE JUSTICE. A Lost Egg who came from the Legions, and was appointed by the Empress to BE THE JUSTICE. Carmela's ally; technically her army actually belongs to him, and she is just the commander. It is important that this be so, otherwise people would ask hard questions like &quot;why is a Threshold Dragon playing warlord on our northern shore? And why have we not killed her yesterday?&quot;</li> <li>Geno Jin - Husumori's nephew, a Bright Young Man(tm) who is Carmela's rival for the position of the Magistrate's favorite. Silly boy thinks it's a competition. At least he's good in bed. Was until recently betraying intelligence on the both of them (for entirely good and just reasons) to...</li> <li>Sorcerer Bandit - An ambiguously-revolutionary ambiguously-dragonblooded sorcerer that has been building an army of demons and ne'er-do-wells and constantly preying on the region. Carmela's all set to get answers from him on what his deal is, because as of the previous update she shattered his army and captured him! Is either abetted or hindered by...</li> <li>Purplesid - Can't remember what their deal is. Carmela can't, that is. I've got a few ideas.</li> <li>Peleps Lili - Carmela's second-in-command. An old, drunk, bitter woman who thinks the Realm's ideals and Immaculate doctrines are a load of crap (but she has flaws, too). A damn fine officer, though.</li> <li>Tough Moli - A mortal monk of the Immaculate Order, long-suffering because all the Dragons from Houses have deserted and she's intensely lacking in resources. Or was, until Carmela offered her assistance. Thoroughly competent. Carmela is totally not gradually corrupting her.</li> <li>Reaches the Sky - A Lost Egg Air Aspect Dragon-blooded monk of the Immaculate Order. Young as the spring dew. Carmela is totally corrupting him. Taught her how to cut spirits in twain, the two of them teamed up to purge disease gods from the refugee camps in the Pahua Basin.</li> <li>Ragara Saveria - Ryo's wife! Currently dealing with Carmela, is providing food and supplies to help manage the refugee situation in exchange for refugee labor. Pragmatic and sharp as a tack.</li> <li>Tachi-Kun - The God of Central Warfare. Possibly(?) Carmela's new best bud?</li> </ul>Future plans include<ul><li>Convince House Contarini and associates that playing blockade-runner to save Quelaana from Mnemon's fleet is anything remotely approaching a good idea.</li> <li>Use magisterial, immaculate and espionage connections to help out the remaining Iselsi on the Isle</li> <li>Figure out if the Sorcerer Bandit was indeed behind the whole poisoning/assassination plot, or if the rabbit hole goes deeper than that</li> <li>Continue making nice with Tachi-Kun and giving him GRAND IDEAS so he won't expose the conspiracy to the Gold Faction</li> <li>Build, train and equip her army of refugees, ne'er-do-wells, mercenaries and rag-tags such that a proper Imperial Legion won't just laugh at them.</li> <li>Use them to engage in GLORIOUS COMBAT and hopefully not die horribly.</li> <li>Figure out how to get a slave collar on Mnemon for... reasons</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-26-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T09:26:53-07:00","id":1068325,"title":"","content":"I think you meant Ragara <i>Saveria</i> for Ryu's wife. Zara is Aisa's cute recently exalted minion! Unless Zara's been lieing to her about everything, in which case... :single tear:.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T11:28:33-07:00","id":1068356,"title":"","content":"PM's are for resplendent wood but if you're waiting on anything from Ascending tell me in the PM.<br /> <br /> Target Numbers are back to 7. 6 is a bit to easy, don't be afraid of a little failure it makes the story more interesting and I'll always give you something for trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T14:07:29-07:00","id":1068409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1068325#post1068325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you meant Ragara <i>Saveria</i> for Ryu's wife. Zara is Aisa's cute recently exalted minion! Unless Zara's been lieing to her about everything, in which case... :single tear:.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly Aisa got the two of their names wrong during their first encounter and everyone has been too polite to correct her all this time. =P<br /> <br /> That or I forgot. Fixed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:54:54-07:00","id":1071282,"title":"","content":"Aiming to be wrapped up by end of Saturday so you can do letters. Posts coming in a few hours!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T17:12:03-07:00","id":1071842,"title":"","content":"Think we're at a wrap for PM's more or less. Feel free to post your IC Letters now and also to send me a PM with which Backgrounds you want to get from the past week now you know how it played out.<br /> <br /> Someone want to explain to me how much XP I owe and what I need to update?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T17:30:26-07:00","id":1071845,"title":"","content":"Generally at this point we just all start writing our letters - and once all the PC letters are out, you'd post 1-2 NPC letters (Ryu, Titus, whoever else Guan has been teasing me will do updates) and we start the cycle again.<br /> <br /> So far, the rule has been ~4xp per letter/month. From the opening post: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One for writing the letter itself.</li> <li>One for revealing details of your character.</li> <li>One for revealing details of your character's setting.</li> <li>One for advancing the Scarlet Sky Conspiracy\u2019s goals.</li> </ol><br /> I think everyone has gotten all four points every month so far. So if you want to keep up that tradition, 4xp each. If you want to change things, then who knows how much XP you owe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T17:47:32-07:00","id":1071847,"title":"","content":"Well write up letters and tell me in the PM also what your XP should be after this round and I'll adjust it! May need a new OOC to do that so that'll happen too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1211-fansibubbles","name":"Fansibubbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:01:54-07:00","id":1072539,"title":"","content":"Updated my letter to actually include information on Florivet rather than merely claiming it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T01:29:48-07:00","id":1074055,"title":"","content":"I still don't see any information on Florivet. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T08:04:53-07:00","id":1074135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998288-ooc-exalted-2-5-the-scarlet-sky-conspiracy-\u2013-an-epistolary-game?p=1074055#post1074055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see any information on Florivet. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this is weird. When I view the post, it's not there, but when I click &quot;edit&quot; it shows up. :/ The same thing happens with any other edits I make to the post - they show up under &quot;edit&quot; but not when viewing.<br /> <br /> Also, loved your letter this month Eura. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's the addendum:<br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> Florivet is a Soul of the End of All Wisdom, concerned with military matters and dirty fighting. It will hate anything high-minded or fancy, and prefers 'good old fights'. Its weakness is that it loves to fight, and is easily drawn into combat - perhaps a plan involving engaging it into combat and slowly retreating to pull it away from Mnemon's fleet, where you can bring more force to bear? At the very least, it should be easily distracted from controlling the winds and into fighting personally in the midst of a larger conflict.<br /> <br /> <i>(The addendum goes on at some length, mostly dry academic information and historical anecdotes about other Dragon Blooded that have dealt with Florivet. One might suspect Aisa of having read several volumes on the subject, and having trouble containing her enthusiasm for sharing. The essential information is all contained in first paragraph above, however.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 04-06-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":